1
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:09,600
Over a century ago, beings that
prey on humans suddenly appeared.

2
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:19,610
Their absolutely overwhelming strength

3
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:24,070
quickly pushed humanity to
the brink of extinction.

4
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:34,500
The surviving humans constructed
three walls: Maria, Rose, and Sina,

5
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,790
which brought them a century of peace.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,420
However...

7
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:48,550
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared

8
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:53,350
and destroyed one of humanity's
walls-and everyday life with it.

9
00:00:55,270 --> 00:00:58,190
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

10
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:02,150
lost twenty percent of its population
and one-third of its territory,

11
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:07,070
and was forced to
retreat behind Wall Rose.

12
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:17,580
In the year 850, the Colossal
Titan demolished another wall

13
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:22,000
and allowed the Titans inside once again.

14
00:01:22,210 --> 00:01:23,420
Eren!

15
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:25,050
Hurry!

16
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:37,020
The entire populace was
evacuated two hours later.

17
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:40,390
Not a single person was eaten by a Titan...

18
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:47,150
...except for the soldiers who fended
them off and died in the line of duty.

19
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,530
Eren.

20
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:53,160
As long as I have you,
I can do anything.

21
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:13,140
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

22
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:18,600
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

23
00:02:18,810 --> 00:02:23,690
Prayers won't solve anything

24
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:29,030
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

25
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:34,320
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

26
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:36,870
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

27
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,750
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

28
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:45,130
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

29
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:50,420
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

30
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:55,640
consumed with surging bloodlust,

31
00:02:55,850 --> 00:03:02,770
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

32
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:29,981
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3

33
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:36,970
Please wait, Captain!

34
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:38,970
Should the Titans attack,

35
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:42,220
we supply soldiers won't be able
to hold this position on our own!

36
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:44,940
Please, Sir! You have to stay here!

37
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,810
Step aside.

38
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:51,860
I must reorganize the
reinforcements now.

39
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:55,740
Behind the safety of
the inner gate, you mean?

40
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:58,280
What the hell are you trying to say?

41
00:03:58,490 --> 00:04:00,330
I'll have you know I'm following regulations!

42
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:03,950
Obeying established
regulations is a soldier's duty!

43
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,120
B-But, Sir!
If we lose this position...!

44
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:08,210
Enough of your talk!

45
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:10,920
Open your mouth again

46
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:15,260
and I'll be forced to punish
you for treason where you stand!

47
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:31,690
Why isn't anyone going over the wall?

48
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,400
I'm sure they heard the
bell signaling us to withdraw...

49
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:52,210
It's all over...

50
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:54,050
We're done for...

51
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:05,220
There!

52
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:08,310
What good is that going to do?

53
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:20,110
C'mon, Jean! What are we gonna do?!

54
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,740
Ain't anything we can do...

55
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:25,200
They finally gave the order to withdraw,

56
00:05:25,410 --> 00:05:28,160
but we don't have enough
gas to scale the wall...

57
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:30,870
We're all gonna die now...

58
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,750
All 'cause of those cowards...

59
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,750
You mean the supply soldiers?!

60
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:39,010
What's happened to them?!
Were they wiped out?!

61
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:41,840
Apparently they lost the will to fight.

62
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,220
I can understand the feeling,

63
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:46,310
but abandoning
their duty to supply us

64
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:49,100
so they can barricade
themselves inside Headquarters?

65
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:51,560
And sure enough,
Titans have swarmed the place,

66
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:53,690
meaning we can't even
get gas for ourselves.

67
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,690
In that case, it's sink or swim!

68
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,400
We'll just have to
take out the Titans there!

69
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:03,530
Hanging around here's no different!
The Titans will just gather here too!

70
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:07,700
We'll only use up what little gas we
have left if we keep running aimlessly!

71
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:11,710
Once we lose our mobility,
we're really done for!

72
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:15,500
You're actually using
your head for once, Conny.

73
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:19,670
But do you really think we
have the manpower to pull that off?

74
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:23,010
Most of the veteran members of
the vanguard have been wiped out.

75
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,300
We're just cadets;

76
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:28,520
who can possibly take charge of
a suicide mission like that?

77
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,640
Even if someone could,

78
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:33,730
it's not like we'd stand a chance
against the Titans anyway.

79
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:39,530
And the supply room's probably got
some that are three or four meters high.

80
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:44,030
There's no way we could
get anything done in there.

81
00:06:44,990 --> 00:06:47,530
It's hopeless?

82
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:50,250
What a dull life this was.

83
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:53,790
If I'd known this would happen,
I would've said something sooner.

84
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,170
Come on, guys! Let's do it!

85
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,500
Get up!

86
00:06:57,710 --> 00:07:01,010
If we all work together,
we're sure to succeed!

87
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:03,260
I'll take the lead!

88
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,270
Armin! Let's go...!

89
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,320
Reiner.

90
00:07:24,530 --> 00:07:25,410
What now?

91
00:07:25,610 --> 00:07:28,910
Not yet. We have to let them gather first.

92
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,740
It's no use...

93
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:34,250
However you look at it,
we're not getting out of this city.

94
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,750
We're all dead.

95
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:40,250
I mean, I'm ready
to die and everything...

96
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:44,630
It's just... what am I dying for?

97
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,630
Mikasa!

98
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,800
Weren't you with the rearguard?!

99
00:07:48,010 --> 00:07:49,430
Annie!

100
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:51,930
I understand the gist of the situation.

101
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:55,100
So I'm sorry for letting
my personal matters interfere...

102
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:57,440
...but have you seen Eren's squad?

103
00:07:57,650 --> 00:08:00,690
I haven't, but some squads did
make it over the wall...

104
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:03,570
Actually, we did find Armin over there.

105
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,740
Armin!

106
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,240
Mikasa...

107
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:13,580
No! I can't bring myself to face her!

108
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:16,710
All I did was survive for
no good reason...

109
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:19,130
If I'd known this would happen...

110
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:22,340
...I would rather have
died with him then instead!

111
00:08:24,010 --> 00:08:24,840
Armin.

112
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:28,680
You're not hurt, are you?
Are you all right?

113
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:36,190
Where's Eren?

114
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,940
Armin?

115
00:08:51,330 --> 00:08:52,740
We...

116
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:57,410
The cadets of Squad 34...

117
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,210
Thomas Wagner...

118
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,340
Nack Tierce...

119
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:03,880
Milieus Zeremski...

120
00:09:04,090 --> 00:09:06,050
Mina Carolina...

121
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:08,760
Eren Jaeger...

122
00:09:08,970 --> 00:09:10,550
These five members...

123
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,430
...fulfilled their duties...

124
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,270
...and died valiantly
on the field of battle!

125
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,940
You can't be serious...

126
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:25,440
So Squad 34 is basically gone...

127
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:29,780
The same thing'll happen to
us if we try to take the Titans on...

128
00:09:29,990 --> 00:09:32,410
I'm sorry, Mikasa...

129
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:36,040
It should've been me, not Eren...

130
00:09:36,250 --> 00:09:37,700
I...

131
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:40,250
...wasn't able to do anything...!

132
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,250
I'm sorry...

133
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,710
Armin.

134
00:09:50,970 --> 00:09:52,430
Calm down.

135
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:56,720
Now isn't the time to be emotional.

136
00:09:57,390 --> 00:09:59,020
Now get up.

137
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:01,560
Marco.

138
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:04,310
If we eliminate the Titans
swarming around HQ,

139
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:08,030
we can replenish our gas
supplies and get over the wall.

140
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,360
Correct?

141
00:10:09,570 --> 00:10:11,610
Well, yeah...

142
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,450
But even with your help,
there's just too many...

143
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:15,740
I can handle them.

144
00:10:15,950 --> 00:10:17,370
Huh?!

145
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:20,160
I'm strong.

146
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:22,920
Stronger than all of you.

147
00:10:23,130 --> 00:10:24,840
I'm very strong.

148
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:29,920
As such, I am capable of
annihilating the Titans there!

149
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,800
Even if I have to go it alone.

150
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:36,180
As for all of you,
you're not only unskilled,

151
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:39,140
you're also cowards and wimps.

152
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,730
You're a real disappointment.

153
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,480
You can just stay here
and twiddle your thumbs.

154
00:10:44,690 --> 00:10:46,150
Twiddle and watch.

155
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:49,480
Whoa, Mikasa!
What's gotten into you?!

156
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:52,490
You're seriously gonna take
on all those Titans by yourself?!

157
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,200
There's no way you can beat them!

158
00:10:54,410 --> 00:10:56,990
If I can't, then I'll die.
It's that simple.

159
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:57,990
But...

160
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,450
If I win, I'll live.

161
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:02,620
And the only way to win is to fight!

162
00:11:03,290 --> 00:11:04,710
Hey!

163
00:11:09,090 --> 00:11:12,220
Your way with words
is the real disappointment.

164
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:15,470
You actually considered
that motivational...

165
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:18,720
I blame you for this, Eren...!

166
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:23,100
Hey! Since when were we taught
to let our comrades fight alone?!

167
00:11:23,310 --> 00:11:26,770
Or do you guys want
to end up as actual cowards?!

168
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:29,440
Never thought I'd hear him say that.

169
00:11:35,610 --> 00:11:40,120
Come on, you cowards,
weaklings, and morons!

170
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:41,450
Those guys...

171
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,040
Damn it...

172
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:46,080
All right, let's do it!

173
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:54,840
Hurry!

174
00:11:55,050 --> 00:11:56,680
Follow Mikasa!

175
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,220
Fight as little as possible!

176
00:11:58,430 --> 00:12:01,010
Get to HQ before you run out of gas!

177
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:04,520
Man, Mikasa's incredible...

178
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:07,150
How can she move so fast?!

179
00:12:07,350 --> 00:12:10,270
No! She's using up too much gas!

180
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,650
She's going to run out right away!

181
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,110
Regardless of our skill,

182
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:17,200
once we lose our mobility
we're completely helpless!

183
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:27,120
She's not her usual,
composed self at all!

184
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,960
She's trying to distract
herself from her anguish!

185
00:12:30,170 --> 00:12:32,750
It's only a matter of time until she...!

186
00:12:37,470 --> 00:12:38,890
Mikasa!

187
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:39,970
Damn!

188
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,180
Jean!

189
00:12:41,390 --> 00:12:42,890
You take the lead!

190
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,520
I'll help Armin!

191
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:46,230
- No, I will too!
- Don't be stupid!

192
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,980
There are still Titans everywhere!

193
00:12:48,190 --> 00:12:50,520
Your skills are needed!

194
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:05,200
Again...

195
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:07,750
It's this again...

196
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:11,790
I've lost my family again...

197
00:13:17,590 --> 00:13:22,010
Do I have to revisit this pain...

198
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:26,270
...and start all over from here again?

199
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:50,710
It's no use. We can't
even get near Headquarters.

200
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:53,920
Unless we're prepared to die...

201
00:13:59,090 --> 00:14:01,510
Crap! He's out of gas!

202
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,550
Stay back!

203
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:07,270
- Tom! I'll save you!
- No!

204
00:14:07,470 --> 00:14:08,890
It's too late!

205
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,980
Stop!

206
00:14:22,490 --> 00:14:24,450
Why couldn't I stop them...?

207
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:30,830
Why didn't I stop them?

208
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,710
If I'd made them stop,
this wouldn't have happened...

209
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:42,260
Am I really cut out for this?

210
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,640
Am I really fit to have
a position of responsibility?!

211
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:54,060
No!

212
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:10,410
This world is cruel.

213
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,910
And...

214
00:15:12,830 --> 00:15:14,330
...very beautiful.

215
00:15:21,050 --> 00:15:23,800
It's been a nice life.

216
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,120
Huh?

217
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,290
Why?

218
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,340
I was sure I'd given up...

219
00:16:06,890 --> 00:16:10,810
Why... am I standing up?

220
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,770
Why... am I struggling?

221
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,070
What for?

222
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:27,160
After all...

223
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,830
There's no point
in living anymore...

224
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,830
So what's driving me?

225
00:16:39,170 --> 00:16:40,590
Fight!

226
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:43,300
Fight! Fight!

227
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:45,760
Eren...

228
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:47,930
Fight!

229
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,390
You have to fight!

230
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,600
Fight!

231
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:53,680
Fight!

232
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,850
I'm sorry, Eren...

233
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,310
I won't give up anymore...

234
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,610
I'll never give up again...

235
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:10,030
If I die...

236
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:13,990
...I'll lose my memories of
you too, on top of everything else.

237
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,410
So...

238
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:17,410
...I'll do whatever it takes to win!

239
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:19,670
Whatever it takes to live!

240
00:17:36,810 --> 00:17:38,640
What just happened?!

241
00:17:59,410 --> 00:18:00,830
A Titan...

242
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,540
...is killing...

243
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,260
...another Titan...

244
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,530
Please, Mikasa!

245
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:34,160
Be all right!

246
00:18:38,290 --> 00:18:39,700
Mikasa!

247
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:52,720
Mikasa! Are you all right?!

248
00:18:52,930 --> 00:18:54,970
- You two okay?!
- Yeah!

249
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:57,220
We gotta get out of here!

250
00:18:59,970 --> 00:19:02,640
Crap! Two 15-meter ones!

251
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,810
No, that Titan is...

252
00:19:08,570 --> 00:19:10,190
Huh?!

253
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,360
I-It finished it off?!

254
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:57,870
It was actually aware of
its weak spot?!

255
00:19:58,070 --> 00:19:59,410
We gotta get out of here!

256
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:00,870
Before it comes this way!

257
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:04,000
No, it's not reacting to us.

258
00:20:04,210 --> 00:20:06,830
Any other one
would attack us for sure...

259
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:10,880
It seemed to grasp the concept
of hand-to-hand combat too.

260
00:20:11,090 --> 00:20:12,590
Just what is it...?

261
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:15,090
All we can do is chalk it
up as an Abnormal!

262
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,800
We barely know
anything about 'em, after all.

263
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:19,720
Now let's just hurry to HQ!

264
00:20:19,930 --> 00:20:23,220
Wait! Mikasa's completely out of gas!

265
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:24,140
Huh?!

266
00:20:24,350 --> 00:20:25,270
Whoa, are you serious?!

267
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,230
Now what are we gonna do?!
We need you!

268
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,110
The answer's obvious!

269
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:32,690
I don't have much left...

270
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,690
...but hurry and
switch yours with mine!

271
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:35,860
Armin!

272
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:37,910
This is our only option!

273
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,870
It'll amount to nothing if I keep it.

274
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:42,490
Just...

275
00:20:42,990 --> 00:20:45,580
Use it carefully this time.

276
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:48,120
Everyone's lives are riding on it.

277
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:55,630
I took charge without any sense
of responsibility for their lives...

278
00:20:55,840 --> 00:21:00,600
For a short time, I had
even thrown away my own life...

279
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:03,970
All for my own personal reasons.

280
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:07,350
I'm...

281
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:09,020
There!

282
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:13,020
Your mobility gear still works,
and I've given you all my blades.

283
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:17,700
All I ask is that you
leave me with this one...

284
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:22,780
I'd rather not get
eaten alive, if I can help it.

285
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,870
N-No way...

286
00:21:31,170 --> 00:21:32,590
Armin.

287
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,630
I'm not leaving you here.

288
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:49,020
Back there...

289
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:53,730
...I was completely confused.

290
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:59,320
I'd never heard of a
Titan killing another Titan before.

291
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:04,200
But I also felt a
faint glimmer of elation.

292
00:22:05,410 --> 00:22:07,500
Because what I saw...

293
00:22:10,250 --> 00:22:13,750
...looked like the manifestation
of humankind's anger.

294
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:41,400
Your dreams are where your heart is

295
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:47,660
They're more fragile than life itself

296
00:22:47,870 --> 00:22:52,330
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

297
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:59,010
Now, rest in peace

298
00:22:59,210 --> 00:23:10,350
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

299
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:20,610
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

300
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:26,570
In this beautiful, cruel world

301
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:31,750
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

302
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:37,460
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

303
00:23:37,670 --> 00:23:43,130
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

304
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:46,760
to anything anymore?

305
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:56,100
A Titan that kills other Titans.

306
00:23:56,310 --> 00:24:02,320
The sight of it leaves the 104th Cadet
Corps Class awestruck and breathless.

307
00:24:02,530 --> 00:24:04,977
What ultimately appears
before them, though, is...

308
00:24:04,977 --> 00:24:06,780
I Can Hear His Heartbeat: The Struggle for Trost, Part 4
What ultimately appears
before them, though, is...

309
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:06,970
I Can Hear His Heartbeat: The Struggle for Trost, Part 4
